From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim Ansell <me@mith.ro>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 11:38:57 +0930
Subject: [PATCH 24/32] Add rp1pio cable driver for RP1 PIO JTAG on RPi 5

On a Raspberry Pi 5 the 40-pin header GPIOs sit behind the RP1
southbridge on PCIe, so bit-banging JTAG through libgpiod costs a PCIe
round trip per edge and loads a 3.8 MB Artix-7 bitstream in ~40 s. The
RP1 has a PIO block that can shift TDI/TDO autonomously; librp1jtag
(https://github.com/mithro/rp1-jtag) programs it and this cable driver
maps openFPGALoader's JtagInterface onto it. Same bitstream: ~6.5 s.

    openFPGALoader -c rp1pio --pins 27:22:4:17 --detect   # TDI:TDO:TCK:TMS

Pins default to the NeTV2 wiring (TCK=4 TMS=17 TDI=27 TDO=22) when
--pins is not given. Build with -DENABLE_RP1_PIO=ON; librp1jtag is found
through its rp1jtag.pc and, when static, its PIOLib backend is linked too.
---
